IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `hvac-nouns`
IMPORT `hvac-law-s6-second-schedule`
IMPORT `hvac-law-s8-validity`
IMPORT `il-interpretation-time`

-- hvac-law-s16-s17-duties-of-licensee.l4 -- Law s 16 (updating details) and s 17 (refresher
-- training).  Quoted from Hebrew Wikisource rev 2947808 (unofficial); the gazette (Sefer
-- HaChukim 3349 pp 185) has the same words.
--
-- UNITS.  Every WITHIN in this file counts DAYS, and the unit is stated only here and in the
-- BECAUSE strings: WITHIN takes a bare number and the language records no unit.
--
-- THE COUNTING.  The two periods counted forward here, s 16's "30 days from the day of the change"
-- and s 17(c)'s extension "not exceeding three months", go through il-interpretation-time.l4 (the
-- Interpretation row's module, vendored unchanged): Interpretation Law s 10(a) (days "from" a day:
-- that day is not counted), s 10(b) (months after an event end on the day with the event day's
-- number, or the month's last day, inside the period) and s 10(c) (days of rest, recess or holiday
-- count in a period unless they are its LAST days).
--
-- s 10(c) IS APPLIED to both (fork F-X1).  Each is a period in which an act must be done -- tell the
-- Registrar; fulfil the training -- and (c) exists so that a rest day does not cut short the time
-- for an act: a period that would end on a day of rest ends on the first day after that is not one.
-- Which days are days of rest is an INPUT, a function from DATE to BOOLEAN; none is hard-coded.
-- A function whose name has no "when days of rest ... are" is the statute with no rest-day input,
-- that is s 10(a) or (b) alone, and is what the first encoding computed.
-- With several days of rest in a row at the end, (c) does not say whether the period is extended
-- to the first day that is not a rest day or replaced day for day; the module takes the first
-- (the Interpretation row's F3, left OPEN there); fork F-X4 here.

§ `Section 16: The duty to update details`

@@Q law 142@@

-- "בתוך 30 ימים מיום השינוי": within 30 days from the day of the change.  Interpretation Law
-- s 10(a): the day of the change is not counted, so the thirty days are the 1st to the 30th day
-- after it and the last timely day is the change day plus 30; a notice on that day is in time.
-- (This was fork F-D4 when the sources did not state the convention; counting the day of the
-- change as the first of the thirty is excluded by s 10(a) and is asserted, and fails, in
-- hvac-tests-red.l4.)  With s 10(c): when that day is a day of rest the period ends on the first
-- day after it that is not one.

-- The calendar with no days of rest: the statute's answer when no rest-day input is supplied.
@ref Interpretation Law s 10(c): days of rest are an input
GIVETH A FUNCTION FROM DATE TO BOOLEAN
`the calendar with no days of rest` MEANS
    `days of rest, recess or holiday listed in` EMPTY

@ref Law s 16; Interpretation Law s 10(a), (c)
GIVEN ch   IS A `Change of details`
      rest IS A FUNCTION FROM DATE TO BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DATE
`s 16: the last day for telling the Registrar of` ch `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` rest MEANS
    `s 10(a), (c) — the last day of a period of` 30 `days from` (ch's `the date of the change`) `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` rest

@ref Law s 16; Interpretation Law s 10(a)
GIVEN ch IS A `Change of details`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 16: the last day for telling the Registrar of` ch MEANS
    `s 16: the last day for telling the Registrar of` ch `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `the calendar with no days of rest`

-- Told in time: the date the Registrar was told is not later than the last day, and the
-- licensee told the Registrar "באופן שעליו יורה הרשם" (in the manner the Registrar directs).
@ref Law s 16; Interpretation Law s 8, s 10(a), (c)
GIVEN ch   IS A `Change of details`
      rest IS A FUNCTION FROM DATE TO BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 16: the licensee told the Registrar in time of` ch `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` rest MEANS
    CONSIDER ch's `the date the Registrar was told`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST t  THEN
            t AT LEAST ch's `the date of the change`
        AND `s 8 — the date` t `is up to and including` (`s 16: the last day for telling the Registrar of` ch `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` rest)
        AND ch's `told in the manner the Registrar directed`

@ref Law s 16
GIVEN ch IS A `Change of details`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 16: the licensee told the Registrar in time of` ch MEANS
    `s 16: the licensee told the Registrar in time of` ch `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `the calendar with no days of rest`

-- Is the licensee in breach on a given day?  Not until the last day has passed without a notice
-- in time: a day inside the thirty days is not a breach even if nothing has yet been said.
@ref Law s 16; Interpretation Law s 10(a), (c)
GIVEN d    IS A DATE
      ch   IS A `Change of details`
      rest IS A FUNCTION FROM DATE TO BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 16: the licensee is in breach on` d `of the duty to tell the Registrar of` ch `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` rest MEANS
        d GREATER THAN `s 16: the last day for telling the Registrar of` ch `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` rest
    AND NOT `s 16: the licensee told the Registrar in time of` ch `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` rest

@ref Law s 16
GIVEN d  IS A DATE
      ch IS A `Change of details`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 16: the licensee is in breach on` d `of the duty to tell the Registrar of` ch MEANS
    `s 16: the licensee is in breach on` d `of the duty to tell the Registrar of` ch `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `the calendar with no days of rest`

-- The duty as conduct.  WITHIN counts days from the day of the change: with no day of rest it is
-- 30, and when s 10(c) moves the last day it is more.  A trace is read from AT 0 as the day of
-- the change.  The BECAUSE string quotes the statute's own words ("30 days"); the count that applies
-- is the one in WITHIN, so a breach record for a period s 10(c) extended says "30 days" beside a
-- deadline of 31 or more.  A DEONTIC cannot be compared in an #ASSERT, so this WITHIN is checked by
-- reading traces (hvac-tests-law.l4) and not by a count.
@ref Law s 16: "בעל רישיון יודיע לרשם על כל שינוי בפרטים שמסר בבקשה לרישיון ... בתוך 30 ימים"; Interpretation Law s 10(a), (c)
GIVEN ch   IS A `Change of details`
      rest IS A FUNCTION FROM DATE TO BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party under the Law` `Act under the Law`
`s 16: the licensee must tell the Registrar of the change` ch `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` rest MEANS
    PARTY  `the licensee`
    MUST   `tell the Registrar of the change in details`
           PROVIDED ch's `told in the manner the Registrar directed`
    WITHIN (Day (`s 16: the last day for telling the Registrar of` ch `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` rest) MINUS Day (ch's `the date of the change`))
    HENCE  FULFILLED
    LEST   BREACH BY `the licensee`
           BECAUSE "s 16: the Registrar was not told, in the manner directed, within 30 days of the change in the details given in the application"

@ref Law s 16
GIVEN ch IS A `Change of details`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party under the Law` `Act under the Law`
`s 16: the licensee must tell the Registrar of the change` ch MEANS
    `s 16: the licensee must tell the Registrar of the change` ch `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` `the calendar with no days of rest`

§ `Section 17: The duty to take part in refresher training`

@@Q law 145 146 147 148 149 150@@

-- s 17(a).  A training counts when it is under the Ministry's supervision, conducted by the
-- Registrar or recognised by the Division, in the licensee's field of practice under his licence,
-- on a date the Registrar directed, and the licensee met its requirements -- and it falls in the
-- last year of the licence's validity.
-- THE LAST YEAR (fork F-V3): the twelve months ending on the last day of validity (s 8).  An
-- attendance is in it when it is not after the last day and one year added to its date reaches
-- the last day.  Where the validity was extended under (c), "the last year of validity" is read
-- as the last year of the validity period as originally fixed.
-- s 10 does not count backwards from a day (the Interpretation row's F8: "before", "preceding",
-- "within N of"), and "the last year of validity" is such a window, so none of the s 10 functions
-- is used here: `add years` is the library's own arithmetic and is not s 10 (fork F-B1).
@ref Law s 17(a)
GIVEN t IS A `Refresher training attended`
      l IS A Licence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 17(a): the training` t `counts towards the duty of` l MEANS
        t's `under the supervision of the Ministry`
    AND t's `conducted by the Registrar or recognised by the Division`
    AND t's `in the licensee's field of practice under the licence`
    AND t's `on a date the Registrar directed`
    AND t's `the licensee met its requirements`
    AND `s 8 — the date` (t's `the date`) `is up to and including` (`the last day of the validity period of` l)
    AND `add years` (t's `the date`) 1 AT LEAST `the last day of the validity period of` l

-- "בהיקף של שמונה שעות לפחות": at least eight hours.  The trainings are plural ("בהשתלמויות"),
-- so the eight hours are an aggregate across the trainings, not eight in one (fork F-T2).
@ref Law s 17(a): "בהיקף של שמונה שעות לפחות"
GIVEN l  IS A Licence
      ts IS A LIST OF `Refresher training attended`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 17(a): the qualifying hours attended by` l `in` ts MEANS
    sum (map (GIVEN t YIELD t's `the hours`) (filter (GIVEN t YIELD `s 17(a): the training` t `counts towards the duty of` l) ts))

@ref Law s 17(a)
GIVEN l  IS A Licence
      ts IS A LIST OF `Refresher training attended`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 17(a): the licensee has done the refresher training required` l `in` ts MEANS
    `s 17(a): the qualifying hours attended by` l `in` ts AT LEAST 8

-- Is the licensee in breach on a given day?  Not before the last day of validity: the duty is
-- to take part "during the last year", so it can only be missed once that year has ended.
@ref Law s 17(a)
GIVEN d  IS A DATE
      l  IS A Licence
      ts IS A LIST OF `Refresher training attended`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 17(a): the licensee is in breach on` d `of the duty of` l `given` ts MEANS
        d GREATER THAN `the last day of the validity period of` l
    AND NOT `s 17(a): the licensee has done the refresher training required` l `in` ts

-- THE LEST BELOW CANNOT FIRE.  s 17(a) states no deadline other than "the last year of the
-- licence's validity", and WITHIN is not used, so nothing expires the duty and a trace never
-- reaches BREACH.  The breach of s 17(a) is carried by the boolean `s 17(a): the licensee is in
-- breach on` above, which compares a day with the last day of validity; this rule shows the
-- standing duty and its discharge, and the BECAUSE string is what a reader would see if a
-- deadline were ever supplied.
@ref Law s 17(a)
GIVEN l  IS A Licence
      ts IS A LIST OF `Refresher training attended`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party under the Law` `Act under the Law`
`s 17(a): the licensee must take part in refresher training` l `in` ts MEANS
    IF   `s 17(a): the licensee has done the refresher training required` l `in` ts
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY `the licensee`
         MUST  `take part in refresher training in the last year of the licence`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST  BREACH BY `the licensee`
               BECAUSE "s 17(a): fewer than eight hours of qualifying refresher training were taken in the last year of the licence"

-- s 17(b): in addition, the Registrar may require a specific training, after consulting the
-- Council, if he found circumstances that justify it and that participation is needed to train
-- the licensee and to realise the purposes of the Law; notice is to be given "זמן סביר" (a
-- reasonable time) before.  Whether circumstances justify it is the Registrar's finding, recorded.
@ref Law s 17(b)
GIVEN r IS AN `Additional training requirement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 17(b): the Registrar may require a specific training on` r MEANS
        r's `the Registrar consulted the Council`
    AND r's `the Registrar found circumstances that justify the requirement`
    AND r's `the Registrar found participation necessary to train the licensee and to realise the purposes of the Law`

@ref Law s 17(b)
GIVEN r IS AN `Additional training requirement`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party under the Law` `Act under the Law`
`s 17(b): the Registrar may require a specific training` r MEANS
    IF   `s 17(b): the Registrar may require a specific training on` r
    THEN PARTY `the Registrar`
         MAY   `require participation in a specific training`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- The notice must be given a reasonable time before the training: a standard of reasonableness,
-- an input and not a computation (it is not a number of days the Law fixes).
@ref Law s 17(b): "תינתן לבעל הרישיון זמן סביר לפני מועד ההשתלמות"
GIVEN r IS AN `Additional training requirement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 17(b): the notice was given a reasonable time before the training` r MEANS
    r's `notice was given a reasonable time before the training`

-- s 17(c): the Registrar may extend the validity of the licence of a licensee who has not done
-- (a) or (b), in special cases and justified circumstances, by a period "שלא תעלה על שלושה חודשים"
-- (not exceeding three months), to do it.  Interpretation Law s 10(b): a period of three months
-- after an event on the last day of validity ends on the day with that day's number three months
-- on, or the month's last day, inside the period; the module's rule agrees with `add months`.
-- s 10(c) is applied (fork F-X1): the extension is the time the licensee is given to do the
-- training, so a last day that is a day of rest moves to the first day after that is not one.
-- That raises the ceiling on the Registrar's power by the rest days; (c) says "the days of a
-- period", it does not distinguish a ceiling from a deadline.
@ref Law s 17(c); Interpretation Law s 10(b)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 17(c): the latest extended last day for a licence whose validity ends on` d MEANS
    `s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` 3 `months after an event on` d

@ref Law s 17(c); Interpretation Law s 10(b), (c)
GIVEN d    IS A DATE
      rest IS A FUNCTION FROM DATE TO BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DATE
`s 17(c): the latest extended last day for a licence whose validity ends on` d `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` rest MEANS
    `s 10(b), (c) — the last day of a period of` 3 `months after an event on` d `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` rest

@ref Law s 17(c)
GIVEN old IS A DATE
      new IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 17(c): an extension from` old `to` new `is within the three months allowed` MEANS
        new AT LEAST old
    AND `s 8 — the date` new `is up to and including` (`s 17(c): the latest extended last day for a licence whose validity ends on` old)

@ref Law s 17(c); Interpretation Law s 8, s 10(c)
GIVEN old  IS A DATE
      new  IS A DATE
      rest IS A FUNCTION FROM DATE TO BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 17(c): an extension from` old `to` new `is within the three months allowed, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` rest MEANS
        new AT LEAST old
    AND `s 8 — the date` new `is up to and including` (`s 17(c): the latest extended last day for a licence whose validity ends on` old `, when days of rest, recess or holiday are` rest)

@ref Law s 17(c)
GIVEN `the licensee has not done the duty under (a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `special case and justified circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar consulted the Council` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party under the Law` `Act under the Law`
`s 17(c): the Registrar may extend the validity of the licence` `the licensee has not done the duty under (a) or (b)` `special case and justified circumstances` `the Registrar consulted the Council` MEANS
    IF       `the licensee has not done the duty under (a) or (b)`
         AND `special case and justified circumstances`
         AND `the Registrar consulted the Council`
    THEN PARTY `the Registrar`
         MAY   `extend the validity of the licence`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- s 17(d): "יראו חובת השתתפות בהשתלמות ועמידה בדרישותיה לפי סעיף זה כתנאי ברישיון" -- the duty
-- is deemed a CONDITION of the licence.  So a licensee acts in accordance with the conditions
-- of the licence (s 3(a)) only if the other conditions are met and the s 17 duty is not breached.
@ref Law s 17(d); s 3(a)
GIVEN `the other conditions of the licence are met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the s 17 duty is breached`                  IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 17(d): the conditions of the licence, including the s 17 duty, are met given` `the other conditions of the licence are met` `and` `the s 17 duty is breached` MEANS
        `the other conditions of the licence are met`
    AND NOT `the s 17 duty is breached`

-- s 17(e): "הרשם יוודא את קיומן, לרבות באמצעות אחר, של השתלמויות, ואת זמינותן" -- a duty of the
-- Registrar, with no time stated.
@ref Law s 17(e)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party under the Law` `Act under the Law`
`s 17(e): the Registrar shall ensure that refresher trainings exist and are available` MEANS
    PARTY `the Registrar`
    MUST  `ensure that refresher trainings exist and are available`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- s 17(f): "הרשם יפרסם ... באתר האינטרנט של המשרד, זמן סביר לפני מועד ההשתלמות" -- publication
-- on the Ministry's website a reasonable time before the training (again a standard, an input).
@ref Law s 17(f)
GIVEN p IS A `Publication of a training`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 17(f): the training was published as required` p MEANS
        p's `published on the Ministry's website`
    AND p's `published a reasonable time before`

@ref Law s 17(f)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party under the Law` `Act under the Law`
`s 17(f): the Registrar shall publish the refresher trainings` MEANS
    PARTY `the Registrar`
    MUST  `publish the refresher trainings on the Ministry's website`
    HENCE FULFILLED
